Medical and clinical sciences (@medical-and-clinical-sciences: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_7HJ8WFCVHVKEB5PT4EWBB8D72E
Medical science investigates disease, injury, prevention, diagnosis, and treatment through biological and clinical evidence. The material connects pathology, immunology, infection, clinical investigation, and the organisation of care, explaining how research and professional practice depend on laboratories, equipment, supplies, and trained teams.

**Reading now:** [Medicine](../Medicine.lingua#r_6DTDCDP6JQ2AV7S78QPGKM2V65) introduces shared medical vocabulary, tissues, body systems, clinical questions, and evidence. Its developed regional sequence continues through musculoskeletal foundations and orthopedics to shoulder anatomy, function, possible problems, and sustained investigation, using English and Portuguese sources.

**Parent:** [Medicine — understanding the body and its care](../Medicine.lingua#r_6DTDCDP6JQ2AV7S78QPGKM2V65).
